# Accessibility (a11y)

- Semantic HTML (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `label`, headings)
- ARIA only when native semantics are not enough
- Full keyboard support; visible focus; logical tab order
- WCAG contrast for text and controls
- Heading levels in order (`h1` then `h2`, no skipped levels)
- Every interactive control must be reachable and named
- Errors announced accessibly (associated with fields, not only color)

```tsx
<label htmlFor="email">Email</label>
<input id="email" type="email" aria-invalid={hasError} aria-describedby="email-err" />
{hasError ? <p id="email-err">Enter a valid email.</p> : null}
```
